# Face Yourself copies the original characteristics of a token (the ruling): Bot2's three 1/1 Rabbit tokens, one of
# them enchanted with Rancor (a 3/1 with trample). Bot1's three copies are 1/1 Rabbits without the Aura's bonus and
# without trample, each with haste: attacking, they deal 3, not 5 (the enchanted token's copy is a 1/1).
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x3
Face Yourself
Mountain x3
Mountain x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus x2
Hop to It
Rancor
Forest x4
Forest x10
[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Hand.Hop to It.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Rancor.Cast(Rabbit Token#1)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Face Yourself.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rabbit Token#1.Power = 1
Bot1.Attack(Rabbit Token#1; Rabbit Token#2; Rabbit Token#3 > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Rabbit Token; Rabbit Token; Rabbit Token; Rancor
